&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Show HN: Benzi – A Code Intillegence/Harness Beating Claude Code and CodeGraph&lt;/b&gt; — New or updated LLM releases affect tool choices across your entire stack — from IDE copilots to pipeline automation. &lt;a href="https://benzi.fly.dev/benchmark"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Any Nix package, live in your browser&lt;/b&gt; — Rust/WASM continue to gain production adoption — worth knowing what's newly ergonomic. &lt;a href="https://simonwillison.net/2026/Sep/10/trynix/"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Show HN: Swiftime - time tracking you can talk to, with an API for AI agents&lt;/b&gt; — Community-vetted signal from Hacker News — high upvote-to-age ratio means the engineering community found it worth reading. &lt;a href="https://swiftime.ai/"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Introducing the Agents API&lt;/b&gt; — Expanding what LLMs can interact with — relevant if you're building or using agentic pipelines. &lt;a href="https://openai.com/index/introducing-the-agents-api"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
